{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting","id":1023210,"title":"How many mages are in your setting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-28T05:47:49-08:00","id":1023210,"title":"How many mages are in your setting?","content":"As the title says. How many mages populate your world? A couple of Hundred for every consilium, or a couple of dozen? What about the Seers? <br /> I'm interested to hear about your worlds and how your PCs interact with NPCs. trying to get ideas for running a game...<br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11055-kaltharion","name":"Kaltharion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T05:53:31-08:00","id":1023212,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/995472-how-many-mages-do-you-see-in-a-single-place\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...a-single-place</a><br /> <br /> People ask this question all the time, there are multiple versions of this thread already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T06:16:53-08:00","id":1023225,"title":"","content":"Ah... thank you. Sorry about cluttering the boards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11055-kaltharion","name":"Kaltharion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T18:44:52-08:00","id":1023533,"title":"","content":"Just one. In my current campaign the PC is the one and only Awakened in the whole area, which is swarming with urban legends, strange phenomena, and management bleeding from an abyssal artifact. There will be some Proximi latter in the chronicle, both on PC's side and allied with Seers but that will be later on. If everything will go according to the plan I will I trounce a Seers or even few of them as a grand final let of the chronicle'so season 1. But I'm playing a tier 1 chronicle intended to have few makes and relatively low power-level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2637-qendi","name":"qendi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T18:52:36-08:00","id":1023538,"title":"","content":"I want to say there's about 40 in the consilium, but it's an odd consilium and there's probably more than that but I doubt anyone in the place could name more than forty. I haven't built them all.<br /> <br /> There's been a lot of traveling, too, and I plan on their being much more so the numbers will vary a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T22:59:21-08:00","id":1023599,"title":"","content":"I tend to follow the 1% of 1% of 1% rule (and not just for Mages) resulting in ~10k mages world wide. This is in part because I run crossover, and keep population counts low so they aren't constantly colliding, but also because I want the PCs and NPCs to feel distinct and rare.<br /> <br /> However, the world has quite a lot Thaumaturges, people with supernatural merits and minisplats running about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T01:12:59-08:00","id":1023622,"title":"","content":"I guess you make your Mages collect in larger cities or otherwise there would only a handful of places that could support more than a single cabal. And that you play in heavily populated areas 'cause here in Sweden we'd only have ten Mages spread out over the entire country. A Concilium would have to cover the entire Nordic area plus the Baltic countries and still would only have about 35 Mages.<br /> <br /> I don't know how many Mages our ST has put in Sweden (where our current campaign takes place) but I'd guess it's around or more than 50 Mages spread out over our ten million population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T01:25:38-08:00","id":1023623,"title":"","content":"I also have a very small Mage population (around 10k, also, about 6k Pentacle, 3k Seers, 1k Nameless). Consiliums/Assemblies are located only in or near major cities or cities of great Mystery and account for a large portion of Mages on that continent. Dispersed Mages within the region can still access the minutes from the meetings and, if there are votes they can participate in, vote by proxy or absentee.<br /> <br /> You'd have two, maybe three, Consiliums/Assemblies for all of Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T01:27:16-08:00","id":1023624,"title":"","content":"Where I live has 6 million+ just in the metropolitan area. So I guess his formula of 1% of 1% of 1% would be only 6, That seems a bit low for 6 million+","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T08:45:48-08:00","id":1023782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1023599#post1023599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to follow the 1% of 1% of 1% rule (and not just for Mages) resulting in ~10k mages world wide. This is in part because I run crossover, and keep population counts low so they aren't constantly colliding, but also because I want the PCs and NPCs to feel distinct and rare.<br /> <br /> However, the world has quite a lot Thaumaturges, people with supernatural merits and minisplats running about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This discussion always reminds me of The Dresden Files as I use it as a very rough supernatural population estimate in many of my CofD chronicles<br /> <br /> There are a lot of miscellaneous minor magical practitioners, psychics, spirits, ghosts and assorted low-level supernaturals, with a significantly smaller, and very feared and respected, amount of A-List supernaturals like vampires, werewolves and mages (e.g, DFs White Counsel wizards).<br /> <br /> Among the teeming supernatural community in the CofD, the vast majority of magic is not practiced by the Awakened, and the Wise are best avoided lest they find you &quot;interesting&quot; and begin to obsess about investigating you further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 12-29-2016, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T10:39:43-08:00","id":1023848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1023782#post1023782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This discussion always reminds me of The Dresden Files as I use it as a very rough supernatural population estimate in many of my CofD chronicles<br /> <br /> There are a lot of miscellaneous minor magical practitioners, psychics, spirits, ghosts and assorted low-level supernaturals, with a significantly smaller, and very feared and respected, amount of A-List supernaturals like vampires, true werewolves and mages (e.g, DFs White Counsel wizards). <br /> <br /> Among the teeming supernatural community in the CofD, the vast majority of magic is not practiced by the Awakened, and the Wise are best avoided lest they find you &amp;quot;interesting&amp;quot; and begin to obsess about investing you further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't have phrased I better myself!<br /> <br /> As to congregation, I tend to run Mages as fairly solitary. Their personalities and obsessions mean that rarely will two Mages really get along, and mysteries can be so fragile that the last thing a Mage wants is another Mage mucking about in their experiments. <br /> <br /> This also means that when you do get a bunch of Mages together it's an important event and in all likelihood they are the only Mages around to get involved, which lends itself well to storytelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T10:45:26-08:00","id":1023849,"title":"","content":"It makes sense in a big brother sort of way. If the mages are rare then that makes them all the more special. And a bigger target for all the little stuff that wants to make a name for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T10:51:05-08:00","id":1023850,"title":"","content":"Boston Unveiled, the official 1st ed. Mage: the Awakening citybook, has 72 Awakened mages in the greater Boston area, of whom about 60 are Pentacle mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T10:52:33-08:00","id":1023852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1023848#post1023848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't have phrased I better myself!<br /> <br /> As to congregation, I tend to run Mages as fairly solitary. Their personalities and obsessions mean that rarely will two Mages really get along, and mysteries can be so fragile that the last thing a Mage wants is another Mage mucking about in their experiments.<br /> <br /> This also means that when you do get a bunch of Mages together it's an important event and in all likelihood they are the only Mages around to get involved, which lends itself well to storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The exception, however, would be cabals. This is necessary for the setting and &quot;realistic&quot; roleplaying to occur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T10:59:37-08:00","id":1023854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1023852#post1023852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The exception, however, would be cabals. This is necessary for the setting and &amp;quot;realistic&amp;quot; roleplaying to occur.</div> </div> </div> </div>My general assumption is that fledgling Mages, especially Free Council Mages, form cabals. But those Cabals almost inevitably fall apart as the Mages drift towards their own obsessions. That or they have huge, potentially violent, falling outs.<br /> <br /> The Diamond favors the mentor student structure, which is no less prone to bad falling out.<br /> <br /> I'll be first to admit this approach probably won't work for most groups, but it fits nicely with my event/arc based style of running.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T11:19:59-08:00","id":1023862,"title":"","content":"Because of how much more spread out the Canadian provinces are population wise the 'local' groups would be more provincial. I have done the same with vampire population but not so much with werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T11:39:45-08:00","id":1023869,"title":"","content":"IMO, it makes a lot of sense for individual Mages to change cabals on a semi-regular basis. Obsessions get completed, the reasons for a cabal's formation can become invalidated, individual priorities change, etc. I haven't looked at the rules for viability on this, but I would also expect Mages to occasionally change Shadow Names to match their new cabal's theme, too. (There was an understated example of this in an AP I read where a bunch of Thearchs decided to make a political statement by forming their own cabal, all with gemstone names... but that was 1e.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T12:41:39-08:00","id":1023894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1023854#post1023854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My general assumption is that fledgling Mages, especially Free Council Mages, form cabals. But those Cabals almost inevitably fall apart as the Mages drift towards their own obsessions. That or they have huge, potentially violent, falling outs.<br /> <br /> The Diamond favors the mentor student structure, which is no less prone to bad falling out.<br /> <br /> I'll be first to admit this approach probably won't work for most groups, but it fits nicely with my event/arc based style of running.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also (should) work alright for crossover - doesn't matter as much if there are only two or three Mages in the area when only one player needs to run one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T13:26:03-08:00","id":1023916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1023894#post1023894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also (should) work alright for crossover - doesn't matter as much if there are only two or three Mages in the area when only one player needs to run one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it works better for crossover. Mages are nosey buggers, and the sort of big plots that facilitate crossover are not well severed by having 40+ random demigods constantly meddling. <br /> <br /> Actually that goes for any event based playstyle (e.g. not week to week city life play).<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, crossover wise, it saves you from having to explain how and why every single major Y-splat is involved in an incident. The easy answer becomes &quot;they aren't&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 12-29-2016, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T18:02:28-08:00","id":1024031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1023869#post1023869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO, it makes a lot of sense for individual Mages to change cabals on a semi-regular basis. Obsessions get completed, the reasons for a cabal's formation can become invalidated, individual priorities change, etc. I haven't looked at the rules for viability on this, but I would also expect Mages to occasionally change Shadow Names to match their new cabal's theme, too. (There was an understated example of this in an AP I read where a bunch of Thearchs decided to make a political statement by forming their own cabal, all with gemstone names... but that was 1e.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In regard to changing shadow names I can see a mechanical way of doing it. Though santity of Merits after you cast off your old name you reinvest it into a new name. Though in my personal preference I'd say to only invest 1 dot there and rebuild the name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T23:15:20-08:00","id":1024134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1024031#post1024031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In regard to changing shadow names I can see a mechanical way of doing it. Though santity of Merits after you cast off your old name you reinvest it into a new name. Though in my personal preference I'd say to only invest 1 dot there and rebuild the name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Now that I've refreshed myself a bit on the rules, I think that the only time it matters is if your Shadow Name has Yantra and Withstand benefits and the dice penalty. I would probably require some transitionary period during which the Merit dots are in limbo, and then just grant them again by Sanctity of Merits.<br /> <br /> And really, it's the Cabal Theme merit that's relevant to what I'm talking about here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T01:29:47-08:00","id":1024152,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> I was more referring to your reference to them changing their shadow name. Both the Merits apply in the way I described however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T03:57:01-08:00","id":1024203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1023869#post1023869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO, it makes a lot of sense for individual Mages to change cabals on a semi-regular basis. Obsessions get completed, the reasons for a cabal's formation can become invalidated, individual priorities change, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>To an extent, however Cabals don't have to be dedicated to the same mysteries. A cabal is primarily a legal structure to organise the Pentacle. Your cabal aren't there to be your friends, they're expected to act as gaurantors of your good behaviour, whilst at the same time acting in mutual defence. There are lots of examples scattered through the books of Awakened who only occasionally meet their cabal-mates.<br /> <br /> The Ebon Noose are an obvious example, the three senior Awakened all have their private obsessions (and don't really seem to like each other much either) but the cabal structure acts to mutually defend them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T10:17:04-08:00","id":1027740,"title":"","content":"Personally I find these numbers too low. There are billions of people in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T12:09:06-08:00","id":1027788,"title":"","content":"There are indeed seven billion people in the world. Of these, about 15 million are millionaires. Those people exercise undue influence over the world as it is. Yet as it stands, there are about 4,000 or so billionaires who more or less, by the strokes of their pens, direct the fates of nations. Some even do so directly, in the cases of Putin and, now, Trump.<br /> <br /> Every single one of those 4,000 bends nations, using something as banal as money, despite being less than 0.00006% of the population. And EVERY Mage has the potential to be one of those, be it by using their magic to attain limitless wealth or bending the minds of politicians or simply rigging elections or outright tinkering with the collective unconscious of humanity. Not every Mage will manage this, but even if one in a hundred does, the truth is that sufficient numbers of Awakened would break setting expectations over their knee or so heavily populate the secret world as to make endeavours by novices all but impossible.<br /> <br /> Trying to keep the setting entirely internally consistent here is pretty much impossible; the players and their lives will always be exceptional.<br /> <br /> The alternative is dynamic equilibrium (a.k.a. the John Constantine's Friend factor), where new Awakened arise constantly but at a rate that is offset by the simple fact that so frigging many of them die regularly as to offset it. The &quot;lifespan&quot; of the average Mage after Awakening may resemble that of a child born in the days before vaccination and antibiotics. This is generally how I've run my settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T13:57:56-08:00","id":1027839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1027788#post1027788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The alternative is dynamic equilibrium (a.k.a. the John Constantine's Friend factor), where new Awakened arise constantly but at a rate that is offset by the simple fact that so frigging many of them die regularly as to offset it. The &quot;lifespan&quot; of the average Mage after Awakening may resemble that of a child born in the days before vaccination and antibiotics. This is generally how I've run my settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's never outright stated, but Boston Unveiled is a good example of that. It's stated that the older members of the consilium like Hydra have seen their entire cabals wiped out before.<br /> The White Putnams, a cabal that's been around for a century are actually presently all the apprentices and apprentices of apprentices of a single mage.<br /> <br /> I kinda wish it was a more explicit element of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T13:58:44-08:00","id":1027840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1027788#post1027788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are indeed seven billion people in the world. Of these, about 15 million are millionaires. Those people exercise undue influence over the world as it is. Yet as it stands, there are about 4,000 or so billionaires who more or less, by the strokes of their pens, direct the fates of nations. Some even do so directly, in the cases of Putin and, now, Trump.<br /> <br /> Every single one of those 4,000 bends nations, using something as banal as money, despite being less than 0.00006% of the population. And EVERY Mage has the potential to be one of those, be it by using their magic to attain limitless wealth or bending the minds of politicians or simply rigging elections or outright tinkering with the collective unconscious of humanity. Not every Mage will manage this, but even if one in a hundred does, the truth is that sufficient numbers of Awakened would break setting expectations over their knee or so heavily populate the secret world as to make endeavours by novices all but impossible.<br /> <br /> Trying to keep the setting entirely internally consistent here is pretty much impossible; the players and their lives will always be exceptional.<br /> <br /> The alternative is dynamic equilibrium (a.k.a. the John Constantine's Friend factor), where new Awakened arise constantly but at a rate that is offset by the simple fact that so frigging many of them die regularly as to offset it. The &quot;lifespan&quot; of the average Mage after Awakening may resemble that of a child born in the days before vaccination and antibiotics. This is generally how I've run my settings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In your chronicles, I guess prudence dictates that old mages are always best avoided if you wish to live a long and happy life. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T14:13:12-08:00","id":1027844,"title":"","content":"Mages in the Wild West: &quot;There ain't room enough if this Consilium for the both of us.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T14:58:54-08:00","id":1027860,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. Of course, old Mages tend to have the coolest toys and best books, so moth meet candle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T15:18:47-08:00","id":1027866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1027860#post1027860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely. Of course, old Mages tend to have the coolest toys and best books, so moth meet candle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd add that if you've seen all your cabalmates, teachers and associates die, that's a pretty good impetus to want to actively go out and teach younger magi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T18:01:51-08:00","id":1027952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1027866#post1027866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd add that if you've seen all your cabalmates, teachers and associates die, that's a pretty good impetus to want to actively go out and teach younger magi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Teach younger magi not to mess with you or your stuff, or they'll be just as dead as your former cabalmates, teachers and associates. Those former cabalmates also got too curious, and you put a quick and permanent end to that... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T02:34:40-08:00","id":1028080,"title":"","content":"I feel like a Rule of Two might be in play here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T21:46:47-08:00","id":1028428,"title":"","content":"No matter how many or few Mages there are in the world they, like normal people, will tend to gather together. They might be drawn by some common mystery, easy access to resources or just the desire for someone they can talk to without the funny looks and calls for the men in white coats. For example the islands of Japan may have only 100 Mages on them and it wouldn't be unreasonable to find most of them living in Tokyo, or at least visiting often.<br /> \u200bIt's the whole reason why they seem to gather in urban centers, instead of the majority being holed up in backwater Montana or the Outback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T07:20:18-08:00","id":1028535,"title":"","content":"A hundred in all of Japan feels exceptionally small. Even in Tokyo, I admit, that feels like very few people, given that the city has a population roughly that of all of Canada. Still, magical resources are what they are.<br /> <br /> As for the presence of the Awakened in urban centres, I'd say that's more a result of serendipity than anything. The Awakened aren't tied to where they were made; they can move. They'll chase Mysteries wherever they can. It's just that urban centres tend to have Mysteries attached to them. Whether this is because even Sleepers are attracted to areas of mystical power subconsciously, whether places with natural resources also tend to have magical ones, or there are simply Mysteries in most places and these are simply the easiest to find is something I am sure the Awakened debate among themselves. Who knows? The presence of enough human beings simply doing their thing might cause Mysteries to appear.<br /> <br /> Awakened may seek each other out for any number of reasons, but the reason they're close enough to do so in the first place is because they're all called by the same thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T11:03:56-08:00","id":1032217,"title":"","content":"I am preparing a new game, with focus on global cold war between Pentacle and Seers. I intend to go with about 1 Mage per 100.000 people, but they aren't evenly distributed - Mages constantly migrate and move from one country to another, forming more or less global community, and most Mages move from their native areas to ones with global Mysteries. There is also a factor that Awakening is more likely to happen in more rich countries with generally more curious and influenced people, and those who awakened in rural Africa or South America tend to move out (some do stay behind and rule their little kingdoms). There is also Seers, who compete for control over most rich and powerful countries and areas of the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T13:30:42-08:00","id":1032297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032217#post1032217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also a factor that Awakening is more likely to happen in more rich countries with generally more curious and influenced people</div> </div> </div> </div>Classism much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T14:16:52-08:00","id":1032318,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, it needs to be pointed out that the entire reason the Seers have whole ministries dedicated to the General or Mammon is because constant strife and poverty are detrimental to the capacity of people to Awaken; they force people to concern themselves with day-to-day survival over access to insight, and limit their ability to educate themselves.<br /> <br /> On the other, yes, there's some weird assumptions in that. For a start, just because there are forces trying to keep people's eyes off the skies doesn't mean there aren't an equal number of forces elsewhere trying to keep people in the dirt. The idea that people are not curious the world over, regardless of wealth, or that people the world over are not susceptible to influence is in direct contradiction to anyone's daily experience.<br /> <br /> Also, while I'm at it, Africa is a continent so large that you could fit all of Europe, the United States, and China inside it and <i>still</i> have room for three extra Britains and maybe an Isle of Man or two. The majority of its 1.26 <i>billion</i> people live in areas along rivers and coasts, meaning that there is a whacking great <i>huge</i> amount of rural and wild area on the continent. The number of Mysteries that are lurking out there are probably uncountable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T18:09:21-08:00","id":1032416,"title":"","content":"STing an ongoing chronicle set in Metro Manila, which is the metropolitan area covering the Philippine capital of Manila plus 16 neighboring cities. The most recent census places Metro Manila's population at 12.9 million not including tourists, people who commute daily in and out of the metro, and the numerous homeless and informal settlers in various urban slums.<br /> <br /> We're currently pegging the local Awakened population at somewhere between 60 - 90 (depending on who's in town) with roughly 30% Diamond, 25% Free Council, 35% Seers of the Throne, and 10% Nameless. This is the political and financial heart of the country after all, and a gateway for visiting mages who wish to explore the Philippines. <br /> <br /> Numbers-wise, this means:<br /> <br /> Diamond Orders &gt; Free Council<br /> Free Council &gt; Any individual Diamond Order<br /> Seers &gt; Diamond Orders<br /> Diamond + Free Council i.e. Pentacle &gt; Seers<br /> <br /> Despite lower numbers, Manila still favors the Seers who have greater access to wealth, resources, and connections in business, church, and government than the Pentacle. While the different Seer Ministries compete, the Pentacle mages also 'enjoy' ongoing rivalries between the Orders, and the Manila Consilium plastering Lex Magica red tape all over the place. The 10% Nameless come into play as 'mercenaries', rivals, or erstwhile allies to Pentacle Cabals and Seer Pylons.<br /> <br /> \u200bHope this helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T05:08:20-08:00","id":1032592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032318#post1032318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because constant strife and poverty are detrimental to the capacity of people to Awaken</div> </div> </div> </div>This. That's why there is less people Awakening in poor countries is lesser per million of people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032318#post1032318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The idea that people are not curious the world over, regardless of wealth, or that people the world over are not susceptible to influence is in direct contradiction to anyone's daily experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not contradiction in my experience. Curiosity is product of being relatively high on Maslow Pyramid; you won't be very curious if you are freezing and dying from hunger, and that's everyday experience of many people in poor countries. So less Awakenings. In my mind, General and Mammon just do their job <i>so much better</i> in those areas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032318#post1032318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The number of Mysteries that are lurking out there are probably uncountable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not arguing with that. Only that there is lesser Awakened people overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T05:42:22-08:00","id":1032601,"title":"","content":"Curiosity isn't a requirement for Awakening. It's pretty explicit that there's a marked tendency for people to Awaken in a crisis. That's literally the central point of the Praetorians, too much violence is likely to trigger Awakenings where low level threats of violence don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T05:49:35-08:00","id":1032604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032601#post1032601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curiosity isn't a requirement for Awakening. It's pretty explicit that there's a marked tendency for people to Awaken in a crisis. That's literally the central point of the Praetorians, too much violence is likely to trigger Awakenings where low level threats of violence don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, given the theme of the game is adicted to mysteries, obsessive curiosity is fairly normal among pre-awakened mages.<br /> <br /> My understanding of why mages gather in cities to pursue the mysteries available there was that it was for much the same reason why normal humans gather together in cities: readily available resources and cheaper living, among others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T06:08:49-08:00","id":1032610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032604#post1032604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, given the theme of the game is adicted to mysteries, obsessive curiosity is fairly normal among pre-awakened mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you mean, but I don't think I agree. I mean, in all the examples, it's an obssession with a specific mystery that leads to Awakening. Also, that obssessive element is clearly not tied to your socio-economic status. Indeed torching your life in the process of chasing the mystery seems a recurring effect of Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T06:09:53-08:00","id":1032611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032601#post1032601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curiosity isn't a requirement for Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I am under impression that curious, open-minded people are more likely to Awaken. Besides, at least two patterns in Awakening require certain degree of freedom of movement and ability to indulge in your obsession, which is rather hard to do then you are working yourself out to feed your wife and kids.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:04:48-08:00","id":1032859,"title":"","content":"Obsession precludes the need to feed yourself and your family. Awakening isn't about curiosity, obsession isn't about curiosity.<br /> <br /> The Labyrinth is a construct to trap curious people in the Lie. Your reasoning that third world countries don't produce as many mages is flawed and incorrect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:35:59-08:00","id":1032884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032592#post1032592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curiosity is product of being relatively high on Maslow Pyramid; you won't be very curious if you are freezing and dying from hunger</div> </div> </div> </div>Curiosity isn't <i>on</i> the &quot;pyramid&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032611#post1032611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, at least two patterns in Awakening require certain degree of freedom of movement and ability to indulge in your obsession, which is rather hard to do then you are working yourself out to feed your wife and kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire point of obsession as addiction is that you're indulging in your obsession <i>instead</i> of what you're supposed to be doing. This means that you can have a wife and kids, but that doesn't actually mean you're feeding them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":2758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","user":"Errol216","date":". 01-16-2017, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:36:45-08:00","id":1032885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032859#post1032859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obsession precludes the need to feed yourself and your family. Awakening isn't about curiosity, obsession isn't about curiosity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't stop you from dying from hunger in the process, or your slave master kicking your brains out the moment you start asking questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032859#post1032859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Labyrinth is a construct to trap curious people in the Lie. Your reasoning that third world countries don't produce as many mages is flawed and incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, and Lie actually works, by keeping eyes on the ground and putting people through horrible lives to make them fear the changes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032859#post1032859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your reasoning that third world countries don't produce as many mages is flawed and incorrect.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't, but we are free to disagree. After all, don't we all have our headcanons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032884#post1032884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curiosity isn't <i>on</i> the &quot;pyramid&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, along with need for self-development, building a meaningful relationships and other things which are really aren't came up on your mind while you are starving and slavering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 01-16-2017, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:55:37-08:00","id":1032894,"title":"","content":"You're right Obsession doesn't stop those things from happening, but as Axelgear pointed out it's canon that excessive violence and oppression also causes Awakenings. Which means when things get bad enough in a third world country you start getting more Mages, not less.<br /> <br /> That isn't what the Lie is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T14:35:05-08:00","id":1032919,"title":"","content":"No matter how many people tend to awaken in poor villages I doubt many will be joining the Pentacle orders. Instead, I think, most will fall into one of two groups. The first group are Nameless Apostates (if they've even heard of the orders) who dedicate themselves and their newfound understanding to helping their friends and neighbors survive and improve their lives in those isolated villages. The second group, those who use their new powers to escape their circumstances, will be snatched up by the Seers. After all, if you are the kind of person who has already abandoned those you've always known will you balk at doing the same to the world at large when someone offers the lifestyle of kings?<br /> \u200bEnd result being that the Awakened World will remain ignorant of most third world awakenings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:20:00-08:00","id":1033020,"title":"","content":"Remaining ignorant of them is completely different from saying that they don't happen. Awakening is explicitly a phenomena that can't be quantified by race, creed or privilege.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T19:07:35-08:00","id":1033093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1023210-how-many-mages-are-in-your-setting?p=1032919#post1032919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bEnd result being that the Awakened World will remain ignorant of most third world awakenings.</div> </div> </div> </div>That implies the Awakened World doesn't have people in the third world, which is just untrue. Each of the Diamond Order books has a section devoted to their positions throughout the world and they are all over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}